{
  "id": "28921_kou",
  "headword": "{乞|こ}う",
  "reading": "こう",
  "romaji": "kou",
  "part_of_speech": "verb (godan)",
  "gloss": "to beg; to ask for; to entreat",
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "to beg; to ask for; to entreat",
      "explanation": "To earnestly request something — help, forgiveness, or mercy — from someone in a more powerful or favorable position. Literary in tone; in everyday speech replaced by {頼|たの}む or お{願|ねが}いする."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "28921_kou_ex1",
      "japanese": "{許|ゆる}しを{乞|こ}う。",
      "english": "To beg for forgiveness.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "28921_kou_ex2",
      "japanese": "{次|つぎ}{回|かい}の{放送|ほうそう}にご{期待|きたい}を{乞|こ}う。",
      "english": "Look forward to the next broadcast. (lit. We entreat your anticipation.)",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "28921_kou_ex3",
      "japanese": "{戦争|せんそう}に{敗|やぶ}れた{兵|へい}は{敵|てき}に{命|いのち}を{乞|こ}うた。",
      "english": "The defeated soldier begged the enemy for his life.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    }
  ],
  "notes": "A literary verb appearing mostly in fixed phrases and written Japanese. Almost never used in daily conversation.\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\nTransitive (takes を). The object is what is requested ({助|たす}けを{乞|こ}う).\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {許|ゆる}しを{乞|こ}う: to beg for forgiveness\n- {命|いのち}を{乞|こ}う: to beg for one's life\n- {助|たす}けを{乞|こ}う: to plead for help\n- ご{期待|きたい}を{乞|こ}う: please look forward to it (set TV/promotional phrase)\n- ご{容赦|ようしゃ}を{乞|こ}う: to ask for forbearance (formal)\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {頼|たの}む: to ask, to request — everyday verb for the same idea\n- お{願|ねが}いする: to request (polite) — standard polite form\n- {懇願|こんがん}する: to entreat — formal Sino-Japanese verb, similar register",
  "schema_version": "2.0",
